  (text "WHY DISCRETE MAGNETICS AND NOT A MAGJACK.\nNeutrik etherCON (H6) is a rugged SHELL around a plain RJ45 — it contains no\nmagnetics at all. So unlike the usual \"HR911105A magjack\" design, the transformer\nhas to be a separate part: T401 (PT61017PEL, 10/100 with centre taps).\nChain: etherCON J401 -> T401 line side -> T401 PHY side -> W5500 TXP/TXN/RXP/RXN.\n\nPOE IS TAPPED HERE, POWERED ON THE POWER SHEET.\n  Mode A (phantom, on the data pairs): T401 centre taps pins 2 and 7\n  Mode B (spare pairs):                J401 pins 4/5 and 7/8\nAll four go to U101 (Ag97005-FL) VINA..VIND, whose internal bridge rectifiers make\nthem polarity-insensitive — which is why no external diode bridge is needed and\nwhy both PoE modes work without a jumper.\n\n*** THESE NETS SIT AT UP TO 57 V RELATIVE TO GND. ***\nPOE_MODEA_* and POE_MODEB_* are NOT logic nets. Keep them clear of signal copper\nand respect creepage to everything on the logic side. This is a SECOND isolation\nconcern, separate from the ADM3053 barrier on the dbCAN sheet.\n\nBob Smith termination: R402/R403 (75R) + C411 (1nF 2kV) to CHASSIS. Terminates the\ncommon-mode impedance of the unused pairs; the capacitor must be a genuine HV part\nbecause it bridges chassis to the cable side.\n\nCHASSIS is a separate net from GND on purpose — it ties to the etherCON shell and\nthe mounting hardware. Decide the single GND-to-CHASSIS bond point at layout, and\nmake it exactly one point.\n\nW5500 notes:\n  Y401 25 MHz is the PHY reference — 10 ppm or better; W5500 needs +/-30 ppm.\n  R401 12.4k 1% on EXRES1 sets the internal bias current. Value is not optional.\n  PMODE0/1/2 pulled HIGH = auto-negotiate, all capabilities advertised.\n  The four LED outputs (SPDLED/LINKLED/DUPLED/ACTLED) are deliberately NOT used:\n  the front-panel LAN LED is driven by the MCU (IO15) so firmware can show richer\n  state than raw PHY activity. The pins remain available if that changes."
    (at 40 150 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.8 1.8)))
    (uuid "f7e49c03-2b0f-442b-bbea-6333eb315b62"))

